      "title": "Lens"
    },
    {
      "description": "Often functions in JavaScript will include comments that indicate the types of their arguments and return values.\nThere's quite a bit of variance across the community, but they often follow the following patterns:\nIf a function accepts another function as an argument it is wrapped in parentheses.\nThe letters , , , are used to signify that the argument can be of any type. The following version of takes a function that transforms a value of some type into another type , an array of values of type , and returns an array of values of type .\nFurther reading",
